---
import '../../styles/handbook-guide.css';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import QuestIcon from '../../components/QuestIcon.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/data';

const topics = [
  { id: 'questbook', title: 'Quest book' },
  { id: 'recipes', title: 'Recipes & workshop' },
  { id: 'character', title: 'Character & skills' },
  { id: 'combat-title', title: 'Epic Fight combat' },
  { id: 'appraisal', title: 'Loot & appraisal' },
  { id: 'claiming', title: 'Claims & travel' },
  { id: 'adventure', title: 'Adventure & magic' },
];
---
<Layout title="In-game tutorial" description="Use the quest book, find pack recipes, build your character and learn the tools you will use in Towns & Kingdoms.">
  <p class="eyebrow"><a href={href('guides/')}>Practical guides</a> / Getting started</p>
  <h1>In-game tutorial</h1>
  <p class="intro">Find your first quest, learn how the pack handles recipes and equipment, and set up a base you can return to.</p>

  <nav class="guide-jumps" aria-label="Tutorial topics">
    {topics.map(topic => <a href={'#' + topic.id}>{topic.title}</a>)}
  </nav>

  <section class="guide-section" id="questbook" aria-labelledby="questbook-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="bookopen" size={28} />
      <h2 id="questbook-title">Find your way around the quest book</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li><strong>Open the Quest Book.</strong> Click <strong>Quests</strong> in the FTB sidebar of your inventory. You can bind <strong>Open Quests</strong> in <strong>Options → Controls → Key Binds</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Finish the in-game Tutorial.</strong> Under <strong>Town Square</strong>, follow the questing and gameplay branches through <strong>Tutorial Complete!</strong> Then open <strong>The Story</strong>, check off <strong>A New Beginning</strong> and claim the eight hamburgers.</li>
      <li><strong>Read the objective and collect the reward.</strong> Item tasks check the requested stack or set and keep your items by default. Tick checkmark tasks yourself. Claim available rewards in the quest screen. Some Story rewards, including character XP and titles, apply automatically.</li>
      <li><strong>Return to The Story between chapters.</strong> Check off <strong>Chapter Completed</strong> on your production board and then its matching milestone in <strong>The Story</strong>. Open the next chapter from <strong>Forging Ahead</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="guide-figure">
      <img src={href('media/tutorial/quest-book-orientation.webp')} width="840" height="226" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Open the Quest Book and choose Story for milestones, Chapters for the workshop, or Market for trading." />
    </figure>
    <dl class="tutorial-boards">
      <div><dt>Town Square</dt><dd>Find Tutorial, The Story, Market, Bulletin Board and Completionist. Start job orders with <strong>Check the Notice Board</strong>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Forging Ahead</dt><dd>Follow ten production chapters to the Creation Core. <a href={href('chapters/')}>Open the chapter questlines</a>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Realms &amp; Relics</dt><dd>Follow exploration, boss, End Remastered eye and useful item quests.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Crafts &amp; Curiosities</dt><dd>Find mod-specific quests for magic, Aeronautics, fishing, everyday life and advanced Create systems.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Seasonal Tales</dt><dd>Find seasonal boards such as <strong>The First Winter</strong>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Completionist</dt><dd>Use <strong>The Golden Collection</strong> to track optional milestones across the pack, including bosses, trades and mod questlines.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>The quest book has 1,539 quests across 28 boards. For the main story finale, see <a href={href('chapters/#chapter-10')}>Chapter X</a>. You can also take a job order from the <strong>Bulletin Board</strong>, then use <strong>Master of Trades</strong> on the Completionist board to track finishing all ten jobs.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="recipes" aria-labelledby="recipes-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="hammer" size={28} />
      <h2 id="recipes-title">Look up recipes and build your first workshop</h2>
    </header>
    <p>Search for an item in JEI and hover over it. With the default bindings, press <kbd>R</kbd> to see how to make it or <kbd>U</kbd> to see what it goes into. You can change <strong>Show Recipes</strong> and <strong>Show Uses</strong> under <strong>Just Enough Items</strong> in Key Binds.</p>
    <figure class="guide-figure">
      <img src={href('media/tutorial/jei-item-lookup.webp')} width="840" height="226" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="With the default JEI controls, hover over Andesite Alloy and press R to see recipes or U to see uses." />
    </figure>
    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li><strong>Start with Chapter I.</strong> Use a crafting table to make a Makeshift Mechanism with four Andesite Alloy, four wooden slabs and one Iron Ingot.</li>
      <li><strong>Build your first Andesite Machine in Chapter II.</strong> Follow <strong>Welcome to the Machine!</strong> and surround one Andesite Casing with eight Makeshift Mechanisms in a crafting table.</li>
      <li><strong>Work backward from the output.</strong> Open each ingredient’s recipe, and check the process and machine before gathering parts. For sequenced assembly, follow the operations and loop count in order.</li>
      <li><strong>See the equipment in action.</strong> Hover over a Create item and hold its Ponder key for the in-game demonstration. Follow the handbook’s <a href={href('tutorials/')}>build guides</a> for complete setups or open the <a href={href('recipes/')}>recipe reference</a>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>Mine a batch with Ultimine.</strong> Hold the bound FTB Ultimine key while mining. Check the highlighted blocks first, then break the target to harvest a batch. The pack caps each batch at 64 eligible blocks, and using Ultimine drains hunger.</p>
    <p>Start with a <a href={href('guides/cobble-generator/')}>cobblestone generator</a>, <a href={href('guides/tree-farm/')}>tree farm</a>, or <a href={href('guides/sapper/')}>Sapper</a>. If a machine stops turning, see the <a href={href('guides/create-troubleshooting/')}>Create troubleshooting guide</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="character" aria-labelledby="character-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="skill_point" size={28} />
      <h2 id="character-title">Build your character</h2>
    </header>
    <p>Open the <strong>Character</strong> screen from your inventory or press <kbd>I</kbd> by default. Look for <strong>Open Character</strong> in Key Binds to change the shortcut. The screen brings together your level, Origin and skills.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Gain character experience.</strong> Fighting, gathering, exploring and quest rewards all support character progression. <a href={href('mechanics/#leveling')}>See the Story level caps and prestige levels</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Choose an Origin.</strong> Read each Origin’s starting bonuses before you confirm your choice. The <a href={href('mechanics/#origins')}>Origins reference</a> shows the full options.</li>
      <li><strong>Spend skill points.</strong> Start at a root and follow connected nodes. You can build across the six professions. Some advanced skills require a minimum point investment before you can buy them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Try a route in the <a href={href('skills/')}>skilltree planner</a>. See the <a href={href('mechanics/#titles')}>title catalogue</a> for milestone rewards, the cosmetic and passive slots, and Eternal Sovereign at level 105.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="combat" aria-labelledby="combat-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="quest_mods" size={28} />
      <h2 id="combat-title">Fight with Epic Fight</h2>
    </header>
    <p><a id="epic-fight-guide" href={href('guides/epic-fight/')}>Open the Epic Fight tutorial</a> for attacks, skills, dodging and parrying.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="appraisal" aria-labelledby="appraisal-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="satchel" size={28} />
      <h2 id="appraisal-title">Open loot and identify equipment</h2>
    </header>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Check your own loot.</strong> Lootr containers give each player their own drops. Everyone in a party should open the Lootr container themselves.</li>
      <li><strong>Appraise unidentified gear.</strong> Bring unidentified equipment to the Identifier and check the experience cost. Later, use the Mechanical Identifier and supported XP fluid for automation.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare the result.</strong> Check the item’s stats, rarity and affixes against your build. Salvaging unwanted gear costs vanilla XP and earns credit toward a later identification.</li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="guide-figure">
      <img src={href('media/loot/mechanical-identifier.webp?style=minecraft')} width="850" height="338" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Mechanical Identifier takes unidentified items from above and liquid experience from the side, then outputs equipment below." />
      <figcaption>See the <a href={href('loot/#automate-identification')}>Mechanical Identifier setup</a> and the full appraisal rules.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="claiming" aria-labelledby="claiming-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="map" size={28} />
      <h2 id="claiming-title">Claim a base and make a return route</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="guide-steps">
      <li><strong>Open the Claim Manager.</strong> Select <strong>FTB Chunks: Claim Manager</strong> in the inventory’s FTB sidebar. Left-click a chunk to claim it or right-click one of your claims to unclaim it.</li>
      <li><strong>Check team access.</strong> If you build with friends, check your team and its access settings before sharing machines or storage. The pack excludes the End and Twilight Forest from land claims and disables force-loading.</li>
      <li><strong>Activate useful Waystones.</strong> Interact with a Waystone to add it as a destination. Visit another Waystone to return to a saved stop. The pack disables the XP cost by default.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The <a href={href('servers/#shared-worlds')}>shared worlds guide</a> covers teams, claims and server travel.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" id="adventure" aria-labelledby="adventure-title">
    <header class="guide-heading">
      <QuestIcon name="potionblue" size={28} />
      <h2 id="adventure-title">Go exploring and learn magic</h2>
    </header>
    <p>Take on adventure quests alongside workshop progression. Pack dimensions use their own entry rules. Check <a href={href('bosses/')}>Boss Encounters</a> for summoning conditions and which bosses drop the eyes you need for the End.</p>
    <p>Build a portal to the <a href={href('guides/aether-portal/')}>Aether</a> or <a href={href('guides/twilight-portal/')}>Twilight Forest</a>, or activate the <a href={href('guides/otherside-portal/')}>Ancient City gateway to the Otherside</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={href('guides/ars-nouveau/')}><strong>Ars Nouveau</strong></a> covers your first glyphs, spell and crop-fed Source setup.</li>
      <li><a href={href('guides/irons-spells/')}><strong>Iron’s Spells ’n Spellbooks</strong></a> shows how to equip a scroll, cast it and use the Scroll Forge.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  function openMovedCombatGuide() {
    if (location.hash !== '#combat') return;
    const guide = document.getElementById('epic-fight-guide');
    if (guide instanceof HTMLAnchorElement) location.replace(guide.href);
  }

  window.addEventListener('hashchange', openMovedCombatGuide);
  openMovedCombatGuide();
</script>

<style>
  .tutorial-boards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }

  .tutorial-boards > div {
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .tutorial-boards dt { color: var(--text); font-weight: 650; }
  .tutorial-boards dd { margin: 3px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }

  @media (max-width: 635px) {
    .tutorial-boards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
